#
# Counter-example for the reasoner-derived measure-and-dimension gate
# (math:DimensionalHomogeneityConstraint, crates/logic/src/reason/math_gate.rs): a
# math:DimensionalExpression combining two math:homogeneousOperand quantities whose
# dimensions are NOT commensurable — one carries the base dimension math:lengthDimension,
# the other math:massDimension, so their exact-rational ℚ⁷ exponent vectors differ (unit
# vectors on distinct axes). The native forward chase over the authored
# math:dimensionalHomogeneityLaw MUST raise math:DimensionalInhomogeneity. Both operands
# resolve cleanly to a real base-dimension vector (no math:MalformedDimension noise); the
# mismatch itself is the single isolated violation.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:mixedSum a math:DimensionalExpression ;
    math:homogeneousOperand ex:lengthOperand , ex:massOperand .

ex:lengthOperand a math:Quantity ;
    math:hasDimension math:lengthDimension .

ex:massOperand a math:Quantity ;
    math:hasDimension math:massDimension .
